  "response": "**VERDICT: REVISE**\n\n**Overall Assessment**: The carousel component implements basic interactive controls but fails to communicate dynamic state changes or structural context to assistive technology. While native `<button>` elements handle focus and activation correctly, the absence of a live region for image updates, missing landmark/region labeling on the container, and lack of active-state communication on indicators break the core interaction model for screen reader users. The design is 60% complete per the WAI-ARIA Slideshow pattern.\n\n**Pre-commitment Predictions**: Based on the component type (dynamic image carousel/slideshow), I predicted:\n1. Missing `aria-live` region for dynamic content announcements\n2. Container lacks semantic grouping/landmark labeling (`role=\"group\"` or `region`)\n3. Indicator buttons lack active-state communication to AT (`aria-current` or `aria-pressed`)\n4. Focus management design undefined for state changes\n5. Generic `alt` text that doesn't scale with dynamic updates\n\nActual findings confirmed all 5 predictions. The component is structurally sound but functionally blind to assistive technology during interaction.\n\n**Critical Findings** (blocks access):\n1. **Missing live region for dynamic image announcements**\n   - Evidence: `src/components/BuggyCarousel.jsx:21-23` (`<img alt={`Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}`} />`) updates visually but no programmatic announcement exists.\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WCAG 4.1.3 Status Messages; WAI-ARIA Slideshow pattern requires `aria-live=\"polite\"` on a status element to announce slide changes.\n   - Fix: Add `<div aria-live=\"polite\" className=\"sr-only\">Image {currentIndex + 1} of {images.length}</div>` inside the carousel container. Update this region's text whenever `currentIndex` changes.\n\n2. **Carousel container lacks landmark/region labeling**\n   - Evidence: `src/components/BuggyCarousel.jsx:18` (`<div className=\"carousel\">`) and `:34` (`<div className=\"carousel-indicators\">`) use generic `<div>` with no ARIA roles or labels.\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users, keyboard users navigating by landmarks\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WCAG 1.3.1 Info and Relationships; WAI-ARIA Slideshow pattern requires the container to have `role=\"group\"` or `role=\"region\"` with an `aria-label` describing the set (e.g., `aria-label=\"Product image carousel\"`).\n   - Fix: Replace `<div className=\"carousel\">` with `<div role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Image carousel\">`. Add `aria-label` to indicators container if it functions as a navigation list.\n\n**Major Findings** (significantly degrades experience):\n1. **Indicator buttons lack active-state communication to assistive technology**\n   - Evidence: `src/components/BuggyCarousel.jsx:39` (`className={idx === currentIndex ? 'active' : ''}`) applies visual styling only. No ARIA state updates when `idx === currentIndex`.\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users, cognitive accessibility users\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WCAG 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value; WAI-ARIA Slideshow pattern requires active indicator to have `aria-current=\"true\"` or `aria-pressed=\"true\"`.\n   - Fix: Add `aria-current={idx === currentIndex ? 'true' : undefined}` (or `aria-pressed`) to each indicator button. Remove reliance on `.active` class for AT state.\n\n2. **Focus management design is undefined for dynamic content updates**\n   - Evidence: `src/components/BuggyCarousel.jsx:10-15` (`goToPrevious`, `goToNext`) update state but do not specify focus behavior post-update.\n   - User group impacted: Keyboard-only users, screen reader users\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WCAG 2.4.3 Focus Order; WAI-ARIA Slideshow pattern states focus should remain on the trigger button or move to a designated status element, but this must be explicitly designed (not accidental).\n   - Fix: Document that focus remains on the clicked Previous/Next button after state change. If moving focus is desired, use `setTimeout(() => focusElementRef.current.focus(), 0)` to survive React re-renders. Explicitly document this behavior in component props/docs.\n\n**Minor Findings** (friction but workaround exists):\n- `alt` text uses generic template literal (`Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}`). While functional, it provides no semantic context about the image content. Screen reader users hear \"Carousel image 3\" without knowing what they're looking at. Consider accepting a `titles` or `descriptions` prop to map indices to descriptive alt text. (ENHANCEMENT)\n\n**Enhancements** (best practice not met):\n- Add `aria-roledescription=\"slide\"` to the `<img>` wrapper per WAI-ARIA Slideshow pattern to improve screen reader phrasing.\n- Consider adding a pause/stop control if auto-play is added later; carousels without user-controlled pause are flagged by WCAG 2.2.2 (Pause, Stop, Hide) when motion is involved.\n\n**What's Missing** (gaps, unhandled edge cases, unstated assumptions):\n- **Missing live region**: No `aria-live` or `role=\"status\"` element exists to announce dynamic state changes. Screen reader users clicking \"Next\" will hear nothing until they manually navigate back to the image.\n- **Missing active-state ARIA on indicators**: Visual `.active` class is invisible to assistive technology. Users cannot determine which slide is current without sighted cues.\n- **Missing region/landmark labeling**: The carousel container and indicator list are generic `<div>` elements. Screen readers cannot identify them as a grouped set or navigation context.\n- **Undefined focus behavior for dynamic updates**: React state updates do not automatically manage focus. While keeping focus on the trigger is acceptable, it must be explicitly designed and documented rather than left to framework defaults.\n\n**Multi-Perspective Notes**:\n| Perspective | Alarm Level | Trigger Signal |\n|-------------|-------------|----------------|\n| Screen reader | HIGH | Missing live region, missing region labeling, missing active-state ARIA on indicators |\n| Keyboard-only | MEDIUM | Focus behavior undefined for dynamic updates; no skip link or landmark navigation within carousel |\n| Low vision | LOW | Native buttons meet target size; visual `.active` class may fail in high contrast mode without AT fallback |\n| Cognitive | MEDIUM | Active indicator relies solely on visual styling; no programmatic state to reinforce selection |\n| Vestibular & motion | LOW | No animations/transitions present |\n| Auditory access | LOW | Static image component, no audio/video |\n| Environmental contrast | LOW | Button labels and alt text provide sufficient non-color cues |\n\n**Verdict Justification**: The component fails to implement core WAI-ARIA Slideshow pattern requirements for dynamic state communication and structural context. Screen reader users will navigate the carousel but will not know when images change, cannot identify the active slide via assistive technology, and will lack landmark context for the image set. These are not minor inconsistencies; they break the functional interaction model for AT users. The design requires revision to add `aria-live`, region labeling, and active-state ARIA before shipping.\n\n**Open Questions (unscored)**:\n- Will this carousel ever support auto-play? If yes, pause/stop controls and `prefers-reduced-motion` handling become CRITICAL per WCAG 2.2.2.\n- Are the indicator buttons intended to be keyboard-focusable? If they are purely visual dots, consider `tabindex=\"-1\"` and `role=\"presentation\"` to reduce keyboard clutter, but only if screen reader users can still access them via the live region or group navigation.\n- Does the parent application provide a skip link or landmark structure that already contextualizes this carousel? If not, the missing `role=\"group\"`/`aria-label` becomes more impactful.",
